above or below your purchase price. You lose everything only if the assets are worthless, which is rare for a diversified fund.\n- **Timing:** The fund announces a liquidation date, and cash follows. Until then, you can usually sell on exchange at market price, which may differ from NAV. Notice and payment schedules vary, so check the notice.\n- **Taxes:** In taxable accounts, the distribution is generally treated as a sale of your shares. Gains or losses are measured against your cost basis. Capital gain distributions paid before liquidation are taxed separately. Expect a Form 1099-B.","ttft_ms":5674,"type":"result","duration_ms":6495,"uuid":"99c3b3d4-3183-4266-a029-58e675f74d58","ttft_stream_ms":405,"time_to_request_ms":67,"first_content_frame_ms":405,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0,"credential_expires_at":"2026-11-28T06:36:39.484Z"}
